format 1
adapter scanner 1
scene: outside

target scan-grass
name: A blade of grass
object: grass
references: ref-openstax-bio-photosynthesis
blurb: Grass makes its own food from sunlight, air and water.
fun_fact: A plant uses sunlight, carbon dioxide and water to make sugar. The carbon in that sugar comes from carbon dioxide.

composition:
    {"symbol":"O","note":"from water and carbon dioxide"}
    {"symbol":"C","note":"from carbon dioxide in the air"}
    {"symbol":"H","note":"from water"}

target scan-sun
name: The Sun
object: sun
atomdex: nuclear-fusion
references: ref-nasa-sun-facts
blurb: A hot, glowing ball of hydrogen and helium at the center of our solar system.
fun_fact: In the Sun's core, hydrogen is fused into helium. Those nuclear reactions power its heat and light.

composition:
    {"symbol":"H","note":"fused into helium in the core"}
    {"symbol":"He","note":"made from hydrogen in the core"}

target scan-air
name: Air
object: air
references: ref-nasa-earth-facts
blurb: Invisible, but it is a mixture of gases.
fun_fact: Near the surface, air is mostly nitrogen, with oxygen next. The rest includes argon, carbon dioxide and neon.

composition:
    {"symbol":"N","note":"by far the most common gas"}
    {"symbol":"O","note":"the gas you breathe"}
    {"symbol":"Ar","note":"a noble gas"}
    {"symbol":"C","note":"in carbon dioxide"}
